/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551192 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551192 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551192 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc125dcb-0e32-5fe9-99db-6daa9af7ad33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112093" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1071 "In a factory, the cost of producing an item depends on the number of items produced per day. The function $U(x)$ models the cost, in dollars, to produce an item if the factory is producing $x$ items per day. What is the best interpretation of ${U}^{′}(500)=0.01?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fdd627b-10f3-56fb-8e8b-56c0cb38ac41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551276 #edb/ref 1074 "The function ${U}^{′}(x)$ represents the rate at which the cost changes when the factory produces $x$ items per day. \n\nTherefore, ${U}^{′}(500)=0.01$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *When the factory produces $500$ items per day, the cost per item increases at a rate of $0.01$ dollars per item*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1071 "Joseph is measuring the weight gain of his pet puppy by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in days, since he started his observations:\n\n- $W(t)$ - The puppy's weight, in kilograms\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the puppy's weight is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99da720f-6132-59c4-9760-cafcb4cb789a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551314 #edb/ref 1074 "The function $W(t)$ gives the weight of the puppy after $t$ days. Then,\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}W(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }W}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${W}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the weight of the puppy increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $W(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${W}^{′}(t)=r(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551363 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551363 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07f8cfdb-1228-53ea-a11d-e93a63c8a9d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551363 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551418 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "833fadcd-bbd6-5042-880a-037df6a6b074" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551418 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551433 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551433 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7ac6ece-a433-5e83-bad9-de6b76cd1d2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551433 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329911 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
